### Part 3: Layer Layout & Blending Styles

Write the styles defining the canvas layers, blending modes, and container constraints:

```css
body {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  background-color: #131314;
  overflow: hidden;
  height: 100vh;
  width: 100vw;
}

.canvas-container-root {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  height: 500px;
  background: transparent;
  pointer-events: none;
  z-index: 1;
  opacity: var(--canvas-opacity);
  transform: translateY(var(--canvas-y));
  transition: opacity 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1), transform 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
}

@media screen and (max-width: 959.98px) {
  .canvas-container-root {
    position: fixed;
    z-index: 1;
    overflow: hidden;
    max-width: 100%;
    --canvas-y: 0px;
  }
}

.nl-canvas {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
}

.nl-bg-layer,
.nl-fg-layer {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
}

.nl-bg-layer {
  opacity: var(--bg-opacity);
}

.nl-fg-layer {
  opacity: var(--fg-opacity);
  mix-blend-mode: screen; /* Blends foreground shape values on screen */
}
```

